{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EqkWv6DF76qfGr35NxCyq6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016AQnW15LtY1dFv2bks7JPF","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/log.md","old_string":"**Summary**: Added a batched CUDA kernel where each block handles one degenerate window, all atomically accumulating into a shared output buffer. This replaced ~10,348 individual kernel launches (each with fill_zero + H2D + kernel + D2H sync) with a single launch cycle. The STARK excl trace APC 300/APC 0 scaling ratio improved from 1.153 (baseline) to 1.022, achieving near-parity. Combined with the previous Round 0 optimization, cumulative STARK excl trace improvement at APC 300 is 283ms (11.4%).","new_string":"**Summary**: Added a batched CUDA kernel where each block handles one degenerate window, all atomically accumulating into a shared output buffer. This replaced ~10,348 individual kernel launches (each with fill_zero + H2D + kernel + D2H sync) with a single launch cycle. The STARK excl trace APC 300/APC 0 scaling ratio improved from 1.153 (baseline) to 1.022, achieving near-parity. Combined with the previous Round 0 optimization, cumulative STARK excl trace improvement at APC 300 is 283ms (11.4%).\n\n## 2026-04-10-2049-batch-round0-coset-parallel\n\n**Idea**: Batch ~935 sequential coset-parallel kernel launches in Round 0 (zerocheck + logup) into 2 batched kernel launches using per-AIR metadata.\n\n**Result**: unmeasured — pre-existing GPU OOM in gkr_input::log_gkr_input_evals prevents pairing benchmark from completing (confirmed on unmodified code). All 94 unit tests pass.\n\n**Summary**: Implemented batched coset-parallel kernels for both zerocheck and logup Round 0 evaluation. Each batched kernel processes all small AIRs (GLOBAL=false, buffer_size ≤ 16) simultaneously via per-AIR metadata structs and a 2D grid with air_for_block mapping. Added a 128 MB memory budget check that disables batching when skip_domain is large to prevent GPU OOM. The optimization is correct (94/94 tests pass) but could not be benchmarked due to a pre-existing OOM bug unrelated to Round 0."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":117,"cache_read_input_tokens":221104,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":117},"output_tokens":66,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"297e37a8-7de7-4f8d-9cb1-f45048fd2150","uuid":"c63fd1f7-2cce-4f05-93d8-188539628815"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016AQnW15LtY1dFv2bks7JPF","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/log.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"297e37a8-7de7-4f8d-9cb1-f45048fd2150","uuid":"bb02e3e7-9d0b-4403-ae7b-1d5659ff55ba","timestamp":"2026-04-10T23:03:57.710Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/log.md","oldString":"**Summary**: Added a batched CUDA kernel where each block handles one degenerate window, all atomically accumulating into a shared output buffer. This replaced ~10,348 individual kernel launches (each with fill_zero + H2D + kernel + D2H sync) with a single launch cycle. The STARK excl trace APC 300/APC 0 scaling ratio improved from 1.153 (baseline) to 1.022, achieving near-parity. Combined with the previous Round 0 optimization, cumulative STARK excl trace improvement at APC 300 is 283ms (11.4%).","newString":"**Summary**: Added a batched CUDA kernel where each block handles one degenerate window, all atomically accumulating into a shared output buffer. This replaced ~10,348 individual kernel launches (each with fill_zero + H2D + kernel + D2H sync) with a single launch cycle. The STARK excl trace APC 300/APC 0 scaling ratio improved from 1.153 (baseline) to 1.022, achieving near-parity. Combined with the previous Round 0 optimization, cumulative STARK excl trace improvement at APC 300 is 283ms (11.4%).\n\n## 2026-04-10-2049-batch-round0-coset-parallel\n\n**Idea**: Batch ~935 sequential coset-parallel kernel launches in Round 0 (zerocheck + logup) into 2 batched kernel launches using per-AIR metadata.\n\n**Result**: unmeasured — pre-existing GPU OOM in gkr_input::log_gkr_input_evals prevents pairing benchmark from completing (confirmed on unmodified code). All 94 unit tests pass.\n\n**Summary**: Implemented batched coset-parallel kernels for both zerocheck and logup Round 0 evaluation. Each batched kernel processes all small AIRs (GLOBAL=false, buffer_size ≤ 16) simultaneously via per-AIR metadata structs and a 2D grid with air_for_block mapping. Added a 128 MB memory budget check that disables batching when skip_domain is large to prevent GPU OOM. The optimization is correct (94/94 tests pass) but could not be benchmarked due to a pre-existing OOM bug unrelated to Round 0.","originalFile":"# AutoOpt Log\n\n## 2026-04-10-1933-defer-round0-d2h-sync\n\n**Idea**: Defer D2H synchronization in Round 0 by splitting the per-AIR loop into a GPU launch phase and a CPU processing phase, eliminating ~1,246 blocking sync points.\n\n**Result**: success — STARK excl trace APC 300: -104ms vs baseline (2478ms -> 2374ms, 1.04x lower); Round 0 APC 300: -94ms vs baseline (663ms -> 569ms, 1.17x lower)\n\n**Summary**: Restructured `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` to launch all GPU kernels before processing any results. The improvement scales with APC count as expected (APC 0: negligible, APC 100: -86ms Round 0, APC 300: -93ms Round 0). The absolute savings were lower than the plan's estimate of 200-300ms, likely because CPU-side work in the logup kernel setup already provided partial GPU overlap in the original code. The optimization establishes a clean two-phase structure that enables future rayon parallelization of Phase 2 CPU work.\n\n## 2026-04-10-2145-batch-degenerate-stacked-reduction\n\n**Idea**: Batch all degenerate-window kernel launches in Stacked Reduction into a single GPU kernel launch per round, eliminating ~10,348 tiny kernel launches at APC 300.\n\n**Result**: success — STARK excl trace APC 300: -283ms vs baseline (2478ms -> 2195ms, 1.13x lower); Stacked Reduction APC 300: -161ms vs baseline (308ms -> 147ms, 2.10x lower) (vs previous: -165ms, 312ms -> 147ms, 2.12x lower)\n\n**Summary**: Added a batched CUDA kernel where each block handles one degenerate window, all atomically accumulating into a shared output buffer. This replaced ~10,348 individual kernel launches (each with fill_zero + H2D + kernel + D2H sync) with a single launch cycle. The STARK excl trace APC 300/APC 0 scaling ratio improved from 1.153 (baseline) to 1.022, achieving near-parity. Combined with the previous Round 0 optimization, cumulative STARK excl trace improvement at APC 300 is 283ms (11.4%).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":15,"oldLines":3,"newStart":15,"newLines":11,"lines":[" **Result**: success — STARK excl trace APC 300: -283ms vs baseline (2478ms -> 2195ms, 1.13x lower); Stacked Reduction APC 300: -161ms vs baseline (308ms -> 147ms, 2.10x lower) (vs previous: -165ms, 312ms -> 147ms, 2.12x lower)"," "," **Summary**: Added a batched CUDA kernel where each block handles one degenerate window, all atomically accumulating into a shared output buffer. This replaced ~10,348 individual kernel launches (each with fill_zero + H2D + kernel + D2H sync) with a single launch cycle. The STARK excl trace APC 300/APC 0 scaling ratio improved from 1.153 (baseline) to 1.022, achieving near-parity. Combined with the previous Round 0 optimization, cumulative STARK excl trace improvement at APC 300 is 283ms (11.4%).","+","+## 2026-04-10-2049-batch-round0-coset-parallel","+","+**Idea**: Batch ~935 sequential coset-parallel kernel launches in Round 0 (zerocheck + logup) into 2 batched kernel launches using per-AIR metadata.","+","+**Result**: unmeasured — pre-existing GPU OOM in gkr_input::log_gkr_input_evals prevents pairing benchmark from completing (confirmed on unmodified code). All 94 unit tests pass.","+","+**Summary**: Implemented batched coset-parallel kernels for both zerocheck and logup Round 0 evaluation. Each batched kernel processes all small AIRs (GLOBAL=false, buffer_size ≤ 16) simultaneously via per-AIR metadata structs and a 2D grid with air_for_block mapping. Added a 128 MB memory budget check that disables batching when skip_domain is large to prevent GPU OOM. The optimization is correct (94/94 tests pass) but could not be benchmarked due to a pre-existing OOM bug unrelated to Round 0."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
